{"abstain":true,"answer":"There is no single LLC tax rate. An LLC is a state-level organization, not a federal tax designation. For federal taxes, it can elect treatment as a partnership, a disregarded entity (reporting taxes on the owner’s individual return), or an S corporation. [S3]

State taxes and fees also vary. The document gives California as an example with an $800 annual franchise tax plus an additional tax, but does not provide a percentage rate. [S2] Forming an LLC in one state does not necessarily mean income is taxed there; states generally tax income earned within their state. [S1]

Which state is your LLC formed and operating in, and how is it classified for federal tax purposes? The evidence does not provide enough information to determine your applicable rate.","citations":["S3","S2","S1"]}
